WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.060
Sprinkle salt on cucumber slices.

2
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.000
In about 15 minutes, drops of water bead up on top.

3
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.060
Put limp lettuce in plain cold water.

4
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.780
In about 15 minutes, it can turn crisp again.

5
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:24.040
Nobody pushes the water, and the cells do not pump it.

6
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.220
So how does it move, and which way?

7
00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:30.823
Drop food colouring into still water.

8
00:00:31.523 --> 00:00:33.643
At first, it sits in one spot.

9
00:00:34.843 --> 00:00:38.463
Concentration is how much of a substance is in a given space.

10
00:00:39.363 --> 00:00:42.703
Where the drop landed, the dye is highly concentrated.

11
00:00:43.563 --> 00:00:44.943
Far away, it is low.

12
00:00:46.023 --> 00:00:48.503
The particles are always moving at random.

13
00:00:49.303 --> 00:00:51.703
More leave the crowded spot than enter it.

14
00:00:52.023 --> 00:00:53.163
So the dye spreads.

15
00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:59.933
Diffusion is the movement of a substance from where it is more concentrated to where

16
00:00:59.933 --> 00:01:01.333
it is less concentrated.

17
00:01:02.453 --> 00:01:03.833
Now the dye is even.

18
00:01:04.793 --> 00:01:06.353
The particles do not stop.

19
00:01:07.013 --> 00:01:09.513
Just as many move one way as the other.

20
00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:11.833
So the colour stops changing.

21
00:01:12.817 --> 00:01:17.217
The cell membrane is the thin layer around every cell.

22
00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.537
It is selectively permeable.

23
00:01:20.097 --> 00:01:22.857
It lets some things through and holds back others.

24
00:01:24.477 --> 00:01:28.097
Water, oxygen and carbon dioxide cross easily.

25
00:01:29.097 --> 00:01:33.777
Many dissolved particles, such as salt and sugar, cross much less easily.

26
00:01:35.137 --> 00:01:40.577
Oxygen is more concentrated in the blood than inside a cell, so it diffuses in.

27
00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:45.610
Osmosis is the movement of water across a cell membrane.

28
00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:50.490
Dissolve salt in water, and the water there is less concentrated.

29
00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:54.630
Water moves toward the side with more dissolved salt.

30
00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:59.890
Many dissolved particles cannot follow, so the water keeps moving that way.

31
00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.370
Our model membrane holds back all the salt.

32
00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:06.630
Real ones let some through, much more slowly.

33
00:02:07.533 --> 00:02:09.633
Now the cucumber makes sense.

34
00:02:10.733 --> 00:02:15.873
Salt outside means the water outside is less concentrated, so water leaves the

35
00:02:15.873 --> 00:02:22.113
cells. In lettuce, each cell holds more dissolved particles than plain water, so

36
00:02:22.113 --> 00:02:26.073
water moves in. Neither time do the cells spend energy.

37
00:02:26.693 --> 00:02:28.353
That is passive transport.

38
00:02:28.353 --> 00:02:33.473
Water moves toward more dissolved particles, and the cell spends no energy.
